HST Office: Vietnamese module names in Windows-1258 projects can be called by name.

The source text of a Windows-1258 project is composed on import, but the module name kept its
combining marks, so `ModulTiếngViệt.TínhLương` in the code never found the module and the file's macros could
not run. The module name is composed too; the stream name stays as stored.

License: this upstream file remains under its original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/vba-corpus/make_vietnamese_fixtures.py.
---
--- a/oox/source/ole/vbamodule.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/ole/vbamodule.cxx
@@ -78,7 +78,9 @@
                 maStreamName = aRecStrm.readCharArrayUC( nRecSize, meTextEnc );
                 // Actually the stream name seems the best name to use
                 // the VBA_ID_MODULENAME name can sometimes be the wrong case
-                maName = maStreamName;
+                // HST: composed like the code that names it (ModulTiếngViệt.Sub in a Windows-1258 project);
+                // the stream keeps its stored name
+                maName = VbaHelper::composeSourceText( maStreamName, meTextEnc );
             break;
             case VBA_ID_MODULESTREAMNAMEUNICODE:
             break;
